<div class="path-head"><p class="featured-region">Reading path · 7 stops</p><h1 class="path-title">The Age of Revolutions</h1><p class="path-tagline">Half a century in which subjects became citizens on three continents.</p><p class="path-intro">Between 1775 and 1830 the political world turned upside down. Thirteen colonies defied an empire; France beheaded its king and exported revolution by arms; the enslaved of Saint-Domingue freed themselves and founded a state; and South America's liberators unmade the oldest colonial empire of all. This path follows the chain reaction.</p></div>
<ol class="path-steps"><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolution"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/american-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">1 · Encyclopedia · Event · 1765–1783</span><span class="path-step-name">American Revolution</span><span class="path-step-why">The war and the ideas that turned thirteen colonies into a republic.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/french-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">2 · Encyclopedia · Event · 1789–1799</span><span class="path-step-name">French Revolution</span><span class="path-step-why">The revolution that devoured a monarchy and redefined politics everywhere.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/storming-of-the-bastille"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/storming-of-the-bastille.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">3 · Encyclopedia · Event · 1789</span><span class="path-step-name">Storming of the Bastille</span><span class="path-step-why">14 July 1789: the day the crowd entered history.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/french-empire"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">4 · Profile · 1534 CE – 1980 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">French Empire</span><span class="path-step-why">Napoleon carried the revolution's code, and its armies, across Europe.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/haitian-revolution"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/haitian-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">5 · Encyclopedia · Event · 1791–1804</span><span class="path-step-name">Haitian Revolution</span><span class="path-step-why">The only successful revolution of the enslaved, and the age's most radical act.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">6 · Encyclopedia · Person · 1783–1830</span><span class="path-step-name">Simón Bolívar</span><span class="path-step-why">The Liberator of six nations, and the disappointments of victory.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/gran-colombia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/quito.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">7 · Profile · 1819 CE – 1831 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Gran Colombia</span><span class="path-step-why">Bolivar's great experiment: a united South American republic, and why it broke apart.</span></span></a></li></ol>
